cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Sabline, please cite it as below. The DOI is Zenodo's concept
  DOI for the preprint that describes it, which resolves to its newest
  version.
title: "Sabline"
abstract: >-
  A small programming language in which a function's signature declares
  the effects it may perform, a runtime refuses any effect outside the
  budget an operator grants, contracts are checked by a prover before
  running, and a repository can declare the capability surface its
  programs may have and fail any change that widens it. The reference
  implementation of the Sabline capability format (sabline-spec).
type: software
authors:
